From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi7: 060 在关掉下载窗口之前把 RAM code 送进去

The vendor picks the download command by address - PATCH_START_REQ when the
address is the ROM patch offset, TARGET_ADDRESS_LEN_REQ otherwise
(mt_cmd.c, MtCmdAddressLenReq) - so both images travel over the same ring.
What differs is the order: the vendor loads both and only then asks the ROM
to finish, while this driver sends PATCH_FINISH_REQ at the end of the patch
download and only afterwards starts on the RAM code.

Everything measured on the board points at that window:

  0x05 @ 0x00900000, 12 KB, mode 0x80000009  -> didx 0->4, four descriptors
  0x01 @ 0x00912c00, 12 KB, any mode         -> didx stays 0
  0x05 @ 0x00912c00, 12 KB, any mode         -> didx stays 0
  0x01 @ 0x00900000, 12 KB, any mode         -> didx stays 0

The ring runs only for the patch request, and it does so even in the state
the endpoint is left in after PATCH_FINISH_REQ, so the receiver is alive and
the descriptors are fine; what the RAM request lacks is the window the patch
request opens, which PATCH_FINISH_REQ closes.

diag_late_patch_finish keeps the ROM in download state across the RAM code
and sends PATCH_FINISH_REQ right before the start command, which is the order
the vendor uses.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
---
--- a/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
+++ b/wlan_hwifi/mcu/mcu_wm.c
@@ -320,6 +320,18 @@
 	return mode;
 }
 
+/*
+ * 060: ROM answers TARGET_ADDRESS_LEN_REQ and then never fetches a descriptor,
+ * whatever the address, the size or the mode word, while the very same ring
+ * runs to the end for PATCH_START_REQ.  The vendor picks the command by
+ * address and loads both images before it asks the ROM to finish, so the RAM
+ * code has to go in while the download window the patch opened is still open.
+ */
+static bool diag_late_patch_finish;
+module_param(diag_late_patch_finish, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(diag_late_patch_finish,
+		 "send PATCH_FINISH_REQ after the RAM code instead of before it");
+
 static int
 mcu_wm_load_patch(struct mtk_hw_dev *dev, struct mtk_mcu_entry *mcu_entry)
 {
@@ -414,9 +426,11 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	ret = mcu_wm_start_patch(dev);
-	if (ret)
-		dev_err(dev->dev, "Failed to start patch\n");
+	if (!diag_late_patch_finish) {
+		ret = mcu_wm_start_patch(dev);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_err(dev->dev, "Failed to start patch\n");
+	}
 
 out:
 	sem = mcu_wm_patch_sem_ctrl(dev, 0);
@@ -630,6 +644,13 @@
 	if (is_wa)
 		option |= FW_START_WORKING_PDA_CR4;
 
+	if (diag_late_patch_finish) {
+		err = mcu_wm_start_patch(dev);
+		dev_err(dev->dev, "diag: late patch finish -> %d\n", err);
+		if (err)
+			return err;
+	}
+
 	return mcu_wm_start_firmware(dev, override, option);
 }
 
